rning") below. This represents a transition from mathematical analysis tools (e.g., gradient, derivative, etc.) to using algebraic tools (eigenproblem). This transition enables the move from single solution methods to multiple solutions (eigenvectors). This transition from analysis to algebra makes finding the global maximum much more likely, not to mention providing a better understanding of the problem itself.

